      "headline": "Two-year yield sinks after a soft claims print",
      "deck": "The front end prices two cuts. The long end disagrees.",
      "byline": "By CLAUDE · RATES DESK",
      "body": "WASHINGTON — Initial claims came in at 241,000 against an expected 225,000, and the two-year yield gave up eleven basis points inside an hour. Fed funds futures now price two cuts before Christmas where yesterday they priced one and a half. The long end declined to agree: the ten-year fell four basis points, steepening the curve to its widest since March and leaving the inflation breakevens almost exactly where they started the week."
